  TechniqueSection(
    title: "Why it matters",
    body:
        "The rock eighth groove is the sentence every other groove is a variation of: hi-hat keeps the eighths, snare marks 2 and 4, the kick says where the song leans. If this one sits, the rest of the kit is details.",
  ),
  TechniqueSection(
    title: "How to play it",
    body:
        "Right hand on the hi-hat, loose wrist, every eighth the same. Left hand hits 2 and 4 as a backbeat — louder than the hi-hat, never rushed. The kick lands under the hi-hat on 1 and 3 so that two sounds become one.",
  ),
  TechniqueSection(
    title: "Practice tips",
    body:
        "Play line 1 until the three limbs feel like one hand. Then take the kick variations slowly; the hi-hat must not flinch when the kick moves. Lines 4 and 7 add the open hat and the crash — keep the backbeat in place.",
  ),
  TechniqueSection(
    title: "Where you hear it",
    body:
        "AC/DC \"Back in Black\", most of the Beatles, every pop song with a drummer. Count-in, hi-hat, go.",
  ),
